Which means that anybody who is likely to violate those norms to do things differently, to prepare food differently, to violate, you know, violate norms of. sanitation and hygiene, they posed a threat not just to themselves, but to anybody in the community. So people who seem likely to act different, people who are from foreign lands, it may kind of activate the sense of these people don't do the things that we're likely to do. And so getting back to your question, the idea is that this kind of xenophobic response to people who are different maybe have historically served the function of trying to avoid and keep away people who would violate local rituals and social norms. So some of these things sound like they could be traditions, things that would be passed down from generation to generation, but was there something going way, way back that maybe the humans who prepared food in a certain way just tended to survive,
这意味着任何可能违反这些规范、以不同方式做事、违反卫生规范的人，不仅对自己构成了威胁，也对社区中的任何人构成了威胁。因此，那些看起来可能会做出不同行为的人，那些来自外国的人，可能会激活这样一种感觉：这些人不做我们可能会做的事情。所以回到你的问题，这个想法是，这种对不同之人的仇外反应，在历史上可能起到了试图避开和驱逐那些会违反当地仪式和社会规范的人的功能。所以其中一些事情听起来像是传统，代代相传的事情，但有没有什么可以追溯到很久很久以前的事情，也许那些以某种特定方式准备食物的人只是倾向于生存下来，

